{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/122016-quasi-idigam-chronicles-wolf-blooded","id":122016,"title":"Quasi-Idigam Chronicles Wolf-Blooded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-29T15:07:35-07:00","id":122016,"title":"Quasi-Idigam Chronicles Wolf-Blooded","content":"So I have <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115874-wolves-of-hell-brainstorming-forsaken-inferno-game-possibly-idigam-chronicles\">&quot;satanic&quot; chronicle idea</a> to run <b>Forsaken</b> game, and was really pumped up to see this after the <b>Idigam Chronices</b> to come out, as I would be glad for all the fixes and especially new Wolf-Blooded take on. But Onyx Path now moved <b>IC</b> from July to September and I'm afraid more delays could come up in mean time. So as I got players, and probably my <b>Mage</b> game can go on hiatus, I need the new take on Wolf-Blooded before the devs will end the book. <b>All from now on is fan take on the subject, no way as official spoilers to <i>Idigam Chronicles</i>!</b><br /> <br /> Now I will take the quotes from original Wolf-Blooded article to what we strive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Idigam Chronicles Wolf-Blooded</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We\u2019ve got about eight Tells worked out, though we\u2019re still firming up the mechanics. Some evoke classic werewolf stories and moves \u2014 one can take Urhan form, but must shapeshift when the full moon rises. Another can take Dalu, but runs the risk of kuruth. One regenerates, but suffers penalties from silver like the Uratha.<br /> <br /> Others give a Wolf-Blooded closer links to the Shadow \u2014 one can act as a 1-dot Locus to allow Reaching, though doing so leaves her Open. Another can allow a spirit to speak through her, though she suffers the spirit\u2019s ban for doing so. Another can Reach and bring others with her, but acts like a beacon for spirits when she does.</div> </div> </div> </div>As to general mechanics, I would used the rules for Ghouls from <b>Blood &amp; Smoke</b> as most recent lesser template and GMC compatible. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Here is my Wolf-Blooded rules proposition then...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Wolf-Blooded</b></span><br /> Relatives of werewolves, or humans that uncover they primal heritage. One night they get lesser First Change, and they life is changed forever. Wolf-Blooded have strange powers and curses of werewolfes from legends and movies a like. But they strengh is limited. And there is always risk of full Death Rage when they use them.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Wolf-Blooded Traits</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Tell:</b> Your wolf-blooded has a mad inspiration from Mother Luna/Father Moon in his veins, and it's bestow part of Uratha blessings on you. You have one power based on your ancestry or exposure to Luna's mad light. Tell is both blessing and curse, often leading to more problems for Wolf-Blooded life. There are two kinds of Tells - Flesh-based that are connected to shapeshifting abilities of proper Uratha and Spirit-based that are about perciving and connecting with Shadow Realm of People. Each activation of Tell power cost one Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Primal Urge:</b> Your character gains the Primal Urge trait at 0, allowing him to store and spend Essence. Character is also totally immune on Lunacy effects. This trait cannot be increased with Experiences or time.<br /> <br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Character can learn Moon and Wolf Gifts, but not Shadow ones. But they don't start with any.<br /> <br /> <b>Kuruth:</b> Every Wolf-Blooded, when using his Tell, is risking Death Rage. If not stated otherwise, for each scene ( or about one hour of active power ) make test on Kuruth of character. Character then enter <i>Wasu-Im</i> Rage and need to follow normal werewolves rules on this subject.<br /> <br /> <b>Senses:</b> All Flesh-based Wolf-Blooded have heightened smell and hearing senses. They can use them to tracking, even in Hishu form, just like Uratha. All Spirit-based Wolf-Blooded can perceive Gantlet and Shadow Realm, just like Uratha. For more rules on both kind scenes see <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b> corebook.<br /> <br /> <b>Flesh-based Tells list:</b><br /> <br /> <i>Urhan Moon Shadow </i>\u2013 Choose one Auspice. Under this moon phase your character can assume form of Urhan, stalking the prey, with no Essence cost. On other nights, he can assume Urhan with cost of one Essence. Each hour in this form character is risking Death Rage.<br /> <br /> <i>Dalu of Rage</i> \u2013 When anger, this Wolf-Blooded can assume Dalu form. He must make Death Rage roll each minute he maintains it or he ends in <i>Wasu-Im</i> rage( <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/122016-quasi-idigam-chronicles-wolf-blooded?p=135284#post135284\">see below</a> ).<br /> <br /> <i>Luna's Silver Blessing</i> \u2013 This Wolf-Blooded has regeneration abilities. He can heal one point of Lethal damage for one Essence he spends. Each point used in this way may generate Death Rage in character.<br /> <br /> What do you think about it? Does it sounds enough \u201cHollywood werewolf\u201d to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-17-2014, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T15:45:14-07:00","id":122046,"title":"","content":"I really don't like the idea of Wolf-Blooded learning Gifts. You need Renown to learn Gifts, and I don't think Wolf-Blooded should be able to earn Renown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T21:48:07-07:00","id":122190,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\">Charlaquin</a>,from what I understand a <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/gifts/\" target=\"_blank\">new Gifts system</a>, the Wolf you don't need to learn from Renown. The Moon and Shadow ones are based on Renowns. Maybe I miss read something?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Idigam Chronicle Gifts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The \u201cand a half\u201d type of Gift are Wolf Gifts, natural paths of spiritual development that many werewolves go through. Wolf Gifts work like Shadow Gifts, but characters don\u2019t have to buy in to them. Characters can take Facets with Renown or with Experiences. The Gift of Change and the Gift of Hunting are what used to be Father Wolf and Mother Luna\u2019s Gifts, but again re-focused around what each werewolf does as part of the hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also don't want to give Wolf-Blooded Renowns, only Wolf-Blooded in longer play need some kick, just like Ghouls get Disciplines. Wolfs Gifts only ( previous as Mother Luna and Father Wolf lists ) maybe good for them?<br /> <br /> There is other aspect devs didn't talk with us to this day...<br /> <br /> <b>How Wolf-Blooded - who have behind themselves equivalent of First Change - become full Uratha?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T22:34:42-07:00","id":122203,"title":"","content":"Looks good to me. Definitely not what I'd do with the wolfblooded, but it's not my game. Keep us updated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T22:36:52-07:00","id":122204,"title":"","content":"You definitely missed something. Here's how it works, as described in the article on Gifts:<br /> <br /> Gift: A group of powers (like a Kindred Discipline)<br /> Facet: A specific power within a Gift (like a particular level of a Discipline)<br /> <br /> An Uratha starts out with one Moon Gift (determined by Auspice), two Shadow Gifts (chosen from a list based on their Tribe and Auspice), and both Wolf Gifts. New Shadow Gifts can be bought with experiences.<br /> <br /> Moon Gifts have a 1-5 tiered progression of Facets, and every time an Uratha gains a dot in their Auspice Renown, they gain the next Facet of their Moon Gift automatically. In order for a Wolf-Blooded to have a Moon Gift, they would have to have an Auspice. Then, once they have access to the Gift, they would have to increase the associated Renown in order to gain any Facets in it, and a Gift doesn't do anything on its own if you don't have any Facets.<br /> <br /> Shadow Gifts have five non-tiered Facets, each associated with a different Renown, and every time an Uratha gains a dot in any Renown, they get a free Facet associated with that Renown in one of the Shadow Gifts they know. A Wolf-Blooded would need to have a Tribe and an Auspice to get the free Gifts at character creation, though they might theoretically be able to buy Shadow Gifts with experiences. But again, without Renown they wouldn't be able to gain any actual Facets in those Gifts, so it would still be useless to them.<br /> <br /> Wolf Gifts work identically to Shadow Gifts, except that all Uratha start out with access to them, regardless of Tribe and Auspice. So a Wolf-Blooded could easily have Wolf Gifts. But once again, without Renown, how are they going to get Facets, and without Facets, what good are Gifts?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you mean by how will Wolf-Blooded become full Uratha? The same way they always have, I assume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T00:27:01-07:00","id":122228,"title":"","content":"<b>Idea to consider:</b> Maybe let Wolf-Blooded to buy next Tells after first one on cost of Gifts? This way players that would &quot;want more&quot; could get it, and character become more like Uratha. Also, plaers become more and more familiar with proper <b>Werewolf</b> mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/122016-quasi-idigam-chronicles-wolf-blooded?p=122204#post122204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you mean by how will Wolf-Blooded become full Uratha? The same way they always have, I assume.</div> </div> </div> </div>The logical implications of new Wolf-Blooded are looking rather diffrent. You could be raised in werewolf-connected family, sure, but with new take from <b>Idigam Chronicles </b>your typical human could some time in play had vision of mad Mother Luna and awake inside the woods, naked, and with lambs blood and fur on you. Practicly - you just got your First Change. I can't see this other way now - WB with transformative Tell must have a way to get they power in one night ( mad inspiration ) and to use it instantly ( change shape ). If it isn't First Change, then what's it it?<br /> <br /> <b>Second Change(???):</b> If we assume that Wolf-Blooded get they little FIrst Change when they get they Tell, so how they become Uratha? One day WB thinks &quot;wow, now I'm full werewolf and can change in 5 forms, not just one and go to Shadow Realm and back with easy&quot;? We could assume they got &quot;second First Change&quot;, but it's looks a bit dull to me - you make twice the same thing to get diffrent effects for the character.<br /> <br /> Now thinking about it - maybe based on if Tell is from Flesh or from Spirit, WB get's other part of equation on &quot;Second Change&quot;? Flesh-based Wolf-Blooded, like those desribed by me, got abducted by spirits to Shadow Realm and must return to Material Realm. And Shadow-based WB got they proper First Change. How do you like it? If this way, maybe Uratha has ancient rites that MAY make Wolf-Blooded in to full werewolf?<br /> <br /> I think here about my future chronicle - if players will start as Flesh-based Wolf-Blooded and I want them to become Uratha, what should I do? &quot;You awake naked inside the woods&quot; second times sounds cheap. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/122016-quasi-idigam-chronicles-wolf-blooded?p=122204#post122204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolf Gifts work identically to Shadow Gifts, except that all Uratha start out with access to them, regardless of Tribe and Auspice. So a Wolf-Blooded could easily have Wolf Gifts. But once again, without Renown, how are they going to get Facets, and without Facets, what good are Gifts?<br /> <br /> I will quote once more, with bolding important part...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The \u201cand a half\u201d type of Gift are Wolf Gifts, natural paths of spiritual development that many werewolves go through. Wolf Gifts work like Shadow Gifts, but characters don\u2019t have to buy in to them. <b>Characters can take Facets with Renown or with Experiences.</b> The Gift of Change and the Gift of Hunting are what used to be Father Wolf and Mother Luna\u2019s Gifts, but again re-focused around what each werewolf does as part of the hunt. </div> </div> </div>So as I see, Wolf-Blooded could take new Wolf Gifts if they buy them with Experiences. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-30-2014, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T03:59:48-07:00","id":122263,"title":"","content":"Just for clarity's sake:<br /> - You need to have at least 1 dot in a particular Renown to be able to take Facets associated with that Renown.<br /> - Wolf Gift Facets are linked to Renown in the same way as Shadow Gifts.<br /> <br /> Now obviously you can just ignore that and give access to Wolf Gifts regardless, however it will impact on some dice pools that certain Wolf Gifts use; some Wolf Gifts also have effects that are directly based on the Renown rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T04:25:00-07:00","id":122265,"title":"","content":"Wow, my topic has summoned <b>Idigam Chronicle</b> developer. I'm honored. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As I don't have ( at least for now ) access to Wolf Gifts of <b>IC</b> and this whole system hack is to allow play before book finally come, I will probably use the original Father Wolf and Mother Luna\u2019s Gifts lists from original <b>Forsaken</b> corebook. On quick glanse I don't see other problem than lower Dice Pool for Gifts itself, and as players would run &quot;lesser werewolves&quot; I don't see true issue with that.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim\">Acrozatarim</a>, is buying other Tells after the first good thing in your opinion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T04:28:59-07:00","id":122268,"title":"","content":"Chris isn't the developer, but he did write the Gifts chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T04:52:36-07:00","id":122271,"title":"","content":"Indeed, not a dev, just a writer! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for buying more Tells after the first, it's not something I'd go for as it changes the nature of Wolf-Blooded further, but if it has the right effect for your planned game then it's not like the Onyx Path police are gonna knock down your door and tell you not to do it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T21:40:21-07:00","id":122944,"title":"","content":"I will see what will the game develop. In short spaning chronicle I want to run probably there want be need for new Tells, but it could be interesting twist for longer play of Wolf-Blooded, like support character for Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Another problem to solve: <b>How Wolf-Blooded, mainly those Flesh-based, would get Essence?</b><br /> <br /> Flesh-based Wolf-Blooded in this rules don't have support for any interaction with Shadow Realm. But they use Essence. I was thinking maybe give them one Essence each moonrise ( New Moon is laso counted then as moonrise ). But better would be something less than &quot;you fill your Essence pool by going Death Rage and eating your nighbors&quot; - this should be solution, but only if character is neglecting his normal Essence harvest and denying his werewolf nature. Something like:<br /> <br /> <i>If Wolf-Blooded is without any point of Essence for number of days equal to his Composure, his spiritual side takes over. He goes in to Death Rage and attack any human to kill him, eat him, and nurished by his Essence.</i><br /> <br /> Practilly, denying your wolf inside you could make you serial canibal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T22:16:09-07:00","id":122968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/122016-quasi-idigam-chronicles-wolf-blooded?p=122944#post122944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another problem to solve: <b>How Wolf-Blooded, mainly those Flesh-based, would get Essence?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>See &quot;The Family&quot; in Volume 4 of the Forsaken Chronicler's Guide, or &quot;The Wild Children&quot; from Volume 3 of same, or &quot;The Moon's Curse&quot; (Volume 1).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T01:13:42-07:00","id":123016,"title":"","content":"So looked over it and seeing this would be rather good solution for &quot;Holywood werewolf&quot; Wolf-Blooded:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 A Wild Child gains Essence from eating raw red meat. One pound of meat is equal to one point of Essence. However, if the Wild Child instead eats the flesh of man or werewolf, he can gain three points of Essence per pound, instead. Note that eating too much raw meat can make any character sick. The Wild Child has a limit of pounds equal to his Stamina score in one 24-hour period. If he goes beyond that limit in pounds, he takes one point of lethal damage per pound consumed. </div> </div> </div>it is interesting, because it means that killing a adlut human ( about 40 pounds of raw meat ) would give 120 Essence. That is about 4 months supply. Meat will surely be rotten to this day, but founding fresh <br /> <br /> <b>Essence need and Hunger:</b><br /> <br /> I think I would solve it that yeah, Wolf-Blooded gets one Essence per moonrise, but they also burn one, after each night. That means that they are in constant state of &quot;I'm <b>hungry like a wolf</b>&quot; (<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) every &quot;high moon&quot; ( around midnight) and to use they Tells, they need to hunt for meat. If they don't get it, they can go on Death Rage from Essence <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">depletion </span></span></span>( even in their sleep), and they instincts will get the needed Essence, mostly as bloody murder.<br /> <br /> So they are putted in constant dilemma - hunt yourself every night for a deer or something, stash fresh meat in they fridge like some creepy &quot;human canibal&quot; or deny all your life and found your loved ones as diner for you. Or help real Forsaken and their Totems, and being granted Essence supply by your service. What do you think about this kind of &quot;lesser werewolves&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T06:39:25-07:00","id":133648,"title":"","content":"Next idea: <b>Wolf-Blooded can be &quot;awekened&quot; by Uratha by confronting humans with Lunacy or Gifts.</b><br /> <br /> Explanation: All humanity is in somehow related to any Uratha. But only little percent are true Wolf-Blooded. It is logical something has &quot;awoke&quot; that gift. This thing is primal terror of Lunacy and need to fight for survival. Prospect Wolf-Blooded are hunted by People and putted in &quot;live or die&quot; situation to release their legacy. Many will die confronted with predator Uratha, but some will retires to the Blood of Wolf in him, and leave First Change.<br /> <br /> Does it looks reasonably? I assume this forcing to First Change could probably be sin for Harmony, but also I don't see is as very severe. Maybe Harmony 5 sin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-12-2014, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T05:59:47-07:00","id":135284,"title":"","content":"As <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-red-mist-descends\" target=\"_blank\">new Death Rage rules has been finally spoiled</a>, here are how I see they should translte for Wolf-Blooded. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wolf-Blooded and Kuruth</span></b><br /> <br /> Death Rage is one of most heaviest of burden for both Uratha and Wolf-Blooded, that they share. All Tells are triggering it on longer exposition, showing partially inhuman nature Wolf-Blooded have. In most instance, they go to <i>Wasu-Im</i> rage, only not switch forms if they don't have acces to it. As creature with shade of true Primal Urge ( working as PU 0 characters ), those kin to Uratha they also are bound with Harmony time intervals this takes. When time of it ends, Wolf-Blooded, just like his Uratha relative, goes in to true Death Rage, <i>Basu-Im</i>.<br /> <br /> WIth restrictions on forms, he can only assume closest to Gauru from his Tells, but other rules of Basu-Im stays. This mean that as Primal Urge 0 werewolves, they assume this state on 5 minutes time. She would not remeber what happed to it in this state. But if character kill someone, other Wolf-Blooded and Uratha of her pack also risk going over in to Basu-Im.<br /> <br /> As to triggers, one of most often, beside using the Talles to long, is Essence starvation. <i>If Wolf-Blooded is without any point of Essence for number of days equal to his Composure, his spiritual side takes over. He goes in to Basu-Im and attack any human to kill him, eat him, and nurished by his Essence.</i><br /> <br /> How do you like this take on Death Rage rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-13-2014, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T05:37:37-07:00","id":140449,"title":"","content":"Taking my players comments from our last game session I made a little amendments to the Wolf-Blooded rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/122016-quasi-idigam-chronicles-wolf-blooded#post122016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Kuruth:</b> Every Wolf-Blooded, when using his Tell, is risking Death Rage. If not stated otherwise, for each scene ( or about one hour of active power ) make test on Kuruth of character. Character then enter <i>Wasu-Im</i> Rage and need to follow normal werewolves rules on this subject.<br /> <br /> <b>Senses:</b> - All Flesh-based Wolf-Blooded have heightened smell and hearing senses. They can use them to tracking, even in Hishu form, just like Uratha. All Spirit-based Wolf-Blooded can perceive Gantlet and Shadow Realm, just like Uratha. For more rules on both kind scenes see <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b> corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you think about them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T08:00:20-07:00","id":225082,"title":"","content":"I am starting a Quasi Idigam Chronicle with Wolfblooded as well in a two weeks time.<br /> This was good reading and inspiration, Thanks to all the contributors!<br /> <br /> I think I will build it like this until the release:<br /> <br /> 1: Our game will have standard Experience (and cost) as we dont like the new beats system that much.We will deal with the changes when I have the book and pdf (I think some smart being here at the forums actually made a transaltion of experience and experience-costs.)<br /> <br /> 2: Wolfblooded template (Standard mortal template). Add tells as new advantage. No need to buy the wolf blooded merit.<br /> <br /> 3: On tells: It seem there are at least 8 of these, and they seem to be rather comprehensive.<br /> I will only use 4 potential tells when we start the game based on the stuff we know from the post.<br /> I will only let player start with one tell.If the book states otherwise everyone gets more stuff! Which makes everyone happy!<br /> <br /> 4: I will remove the lunacy from any and all wolf blooded. For me it will not be a tell at this point.If it later becomes a tell we will settle it at that point.<br /> <br /> 5: Player chosen beginning: If they want to be spiritually changed into becoming wolf blooded instead of the good old &quot;your grand mom was a werewolf..&quot; Im good with either. Or any other original twist to it. This will also relate a bit to what sort of tells you get access to (and merits)<br /> <br /> 6: I will not let Wolfblooded characters get any gifts. Not when we start, at least.<br /> I dont want to homebrew the new gifts-system, as we don't know enough details at this point.<br /> <br /> Tell list player can choose from:<br /> <br /> - Dalu change (Willpower to change)<br /> - Urhan change (no moon change needed) (Willpower to change)<br /> - Fetish use (Wilpower to use)<br /> - Spirit numen (reaching) or maybe another numen if it fits the character story as long as it is not too far out-there.<br /> <br /> Most of what we are doing will have some sort of hybrid of the NWoD rules and the GMC updates. The combat writeups on how to handle combat (and Grapples in particular) are much better in GMC for my tastes.<br /> Not such a fan of the &quot;door-system&quot; from GMC or how they handled spirits. So unless this is changed for Idigam we keep that old fashioned.<br /> <br /> Im looking forward to the Idigam Chronicle.<br /> Not so long to go now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}